---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Home">
    <article class="home-bio">
        <h1>Saksham Gupta</h1>
        <p class="subheadline">Project Lead · Oracle</p>

        <div class="bio-content">
            <p>
                Saksham Gupta is a Project Lead at Oracle, where he leads architecture and
                development for platform orchestration frameworks, legacy modernization, and
                performant web technologies. As an IIT Roorkee Computer Science graduate, he focuses
                on systems programming, language runtimes, and compiler design. Through his work on
                declarative DSL design and framework-agnostic rendering engines, he has optimized
                large-scale enterprise services to achieve substantial reductions in CPU usage and
                API latency.
            </p>

            <p>
                He joined Oracle as a Software Engineer, building the Siebel Open Integration
                project from proof-of-concept to beta within twelve months, and was subsequently
                promoted to Senior Software Engineer and Project Lead. He has led the delivery of a
                recursive JSON-driven web component framework that simplified enterprise UI
                extensions, and spearheaded Oracle's migration of core reactive systems to Java 21
                virtual threads. In 2024, his team reached the top six globally in a corporate
                hackathon on Generative AI out of over one hundred participating teams.
            </p>

            <p>
                He has explored operating systems from scratch, building a custom 32-bit UNIX clone
                kernel in C and assembly, alongside developing various parsers, caching utilities,
                and compiler tools. He holds a B.Tech. in Computer Science from the Indian Institute
                of Technology, Roorkee. Saksham now focuses his time primarily on writing deep dives
                on systems engineering internals, looking for the best ways to share technical
                insights about language runtimes and high-performance software architectures.
            </p>

            <p class="blog-cta">
                <a href="/blog">Read the blog →</a>
            </p>
        </div>
    </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
    .home-bio {
        max-width: var(--max-width);
        margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .home-bio h1 {
        font-size: 2.5rem;
        margin-top: 0;
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .bio-content {
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
        font-size: 1.15rem;
        line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .bio-content p {
        margin-bottom: 1.8rem;
        text-align: justify;
    }

    .blog-cta {
        margin-top: 3rem;
    }

    .blog-cta a {
        font-weight: 600;
        text-decoration: none;
    }

    .blog-cta a:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
    }
</style>
